  "notes": "The board the whole Memphis archetype was generalised from, so what this entry adds is the specific things the parent could only average. The tempo span is deliberately the widest in this batch because the research documents two sub-eras and refuses to collapse them: the Mystic/tape run at 62–72 half-time (= 124–144 straight) and the crunk run 1997–2006 at 74–84 half-time (= 148–168 straight). One model spans both, weighted to the crunk centre because that is where the catalogue's mass sits. Harmony is authored as the research states it — long single-chord i drones with i–VI–VII and i–♭II Phrygian stabs and no functional cadence — so `impliedByRiff` is set and the chord part's variety is carried by how long the loop sits on a chord (`chordDurationBeats`) and by a 32-semitone voicing register, not by progressions the board does not play. `halfStepDissonance` is high because the ♭II stab is the harmonic event. The percussion block is the syncopated 16th cowbell the research calls \"the subdivision engine\", which is why `percs.densityPerBar` is the busiest thing in the kit and the hats are not. ⚠ The snare roll is written as 16th-triplets against the **straight** tempo this model counts in; the research's \"32nd snare/hat rolls\" is a half-time count, and 32nds at 76 half-time are between 16ths and 16th-triplets at 152 straight. Same figure, two clocks. ⚠ The research says countermelody is absent on these records. It is held at the engine's variety floor rather than deleted, because a part that never varies is worse than a quiet one — treat `countermelody.densityRatio` as a floor, not a description. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 40 to 37 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 38 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 3. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
